review:83486_r9 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Depuis quelques jours, des taches de couleurs viennent rappeler çà et là que le temps du souvenir et du recueillement est revenu...virtual visit here" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r10 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "pick up a map at the entrance and go at dusk for extra creepiness" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r11 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Best graves to pay homage to: Amadeo Modigliani, Oscar Wilde, Marcel Proust and Jim Morrisson of course." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r12 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Sin duda, el cementerio más bonito de París y seguramente uno de los más chulos del mundo. ¡No os perdáis la del gran Oscar Wilde o la de Edith Piaff!" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r13 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Passez par la tombe de ce bon vieux jim morrison des doors...vous pourrez laisser un message à sa mémoire sur ce bel arbre situé juste en face ;)" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r14 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "This is how I desecrated Jim Morrison's tomb" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r15 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Well show me the way, to the next whisky bar, oh don't ask why, oh don't ask why..." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r16 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "The trend for famous grave sites was started as a marketing strategy in the 19th century, to get more people to be buried here (it obviously worked!)" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r17 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "TRAVEL FACT: Located in Paris’ 20th arrondissement, this cemetery is the largest in Paris and one of the most famous in the world." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r18 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Take a map and beware of the guides that are trying to take you as a customer" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r19 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Imprescindible ir a este cementerio, ya no por las personalidades allí enterradas sino por lo artístico de todas las criptas :)" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r20 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Largest and one of the most visited cemeteries in Paris, this is where you will find World War I memorials and the graves of famous personalities like writer Oscar Wilde and musician Jim Morrison." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r21 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Munissez-vous d'une carte car il est facile de s'y perdre et les sépultures des gens connus ne sont pratiquement pas identifiées..." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r22 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Faire la visite avec beyern, tout simplement irrésistible" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r23 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "The largest and most visited cemetery in Paris, this is where notable personalities (Oscar Wilde, Chopin, Jim Morrison, Marce Proust) are buried.  16 rue du Repos, 75020 Paris. Tours are available." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r24 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Many famous figures lie in this cemetery, from Jim Morrison, to Chopin, to Oscar Wilde.  Try to go on a sunny day and up to the hill to the summit for a beautiful view of Père Lachaise and the city." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r25 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Oscar Wilde's grave is on renovation until november" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r26 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "ambiance de morts..." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r27 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "A must of any photographer !  I love it in the winter when dustered with snow.  Countless great shot to be made (and not only from Jim Morrisson's grave ! )" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r28 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Effectuer la visite guidée avec un taphophile (spécialiste des cimetières), l'excellent Thierry Le Roi (www.necro-romantiques.com) qui propose un safari nécropolitain plein de culture et d'humour" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r29 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Visit Jim Morisson's grave, I didn't and it still haunts me to this day" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r30 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "between life and death!" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r31 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Могила Джима Моррисона - прямо, направо, дальше спросите у аборигенов - могилка очень неприметна" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r32 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Great place for a picnic!  Quiet, beautiful, and benches throughout." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r33 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Ça vaut la peine d'acheter un plan du cimetière" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r34 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Take a map!" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r35 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Éviter les talons aiguilles ou talons hauts les pavés sont redoutables ici" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r36 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Cherchez les tombes connues mais perdez vous aussi dans les anciens carrés à la recherche de tombes étranges ou de détails amusants." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r37 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Venir en métro: ② ③ à Père Lachaise." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r38 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "No trip to Paris is complete with seeing Pere Lachaise." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r39 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Este Cementerio es muy tranquilo, puedes encontrar tumbas muy viejas! Y de algunos personajes de la historia! Si vienes a Paris, no dejes de visitarlo!..." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r40 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Proust was buried in Père Lachaise cemetery. If you entry from Gambeta, go straight and turn right at avenue transversale №2." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r41 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Bring an updated map! From George Melies to Jim Morrison. The place is huge - be awere of the open tombs." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r42 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "impressive..." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r43 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "C’est le plus grand et le plus célèbre des cimetières parisiens. Vous pourrez rechercher les tombes de Piaf, Musset, Balzac, Colette,, Proust, Wilde, Chopin, Haussmann, Bernhardt, Signoret, Morrisson," ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r44 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "You can get a free map at the main entrance." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r45 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Cemitério de famosos como Allan Kardec, codificador do espiritismo, Jim Morrison, cantor do The Doors e Horácio Pinto da Hora, pintor brasileiro um dos mais destacados do Romantismo." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r46 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Defo get a map! Walked around for ages! Edith Piaf was one row behind main drag." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r47 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "The world's most visited cemetery, Père Lachaise is also called La cité des morts - The city of the dead - by Parisians." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r48 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "A beautiful experience you should live if you go to France to show your respect to all the great people that lie there." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r49 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Taken almost 4 years ago. Wilde's thomb." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r50 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Prenez le temps de vous perdre dans des allées et regardez." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r51 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "c'est où on peut encore parler avec Marcel Proust, Edith Piaf, Eugène Delacroix, Charles Chaplin et d'autres grands maîtres de l'art." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r52 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Oscar Wilde is behind the glass now... What a pity(((" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r53 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Many, many dead people here." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r54 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "At the main entrance you can get, free of charge, the 2 plans of the cemetery. Don't buy from the flower shop. Don't get only only one, as it's incomplete." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r55 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Wilde's grave still visible, but unfortunately cleaned from the typical kisses and barricaded by the city hall." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r56 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Big, big, BIG! Do not enter during a rainshower. Not much place to hide! But still, Very impressive." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r57 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "You really need a map. I didn't find a free map at the entrance, so I took a photo of someone's map with my phone. It doesn't help much, though. Do some research on the internet before you go there." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r58 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Если найти памятник Виктору Нуару, и дотронуться до причинного места - можно вернуть себе мужскую силу и успех  в амурных делах." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r59 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Вообразите себе целый город мертвых с улицами и проспектами, каждый склеп подобен зданию с собственной архитектурой.Холмистая местность усиливает впечатление. Не забудьте взять план на главном входе." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r60 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Le Père Lachaise était le confesseur de Louis XIV. Il avait un appartement dans la maison des Jésuites située sur l'emplacement actuel du cimetière." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r61 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Closes at 5:45pm" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r62 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Bring a guide!! Jim is in the 6th district!" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r63 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "The place to be. Enfin, le plus tard possible ! Vous y croiserez Oscar Wilde, Jim Morrison, Marcel Proust, Chopin, Molière, Eugène Delacroix, Édith Piaf, Seurat, Pissaro, Modigliani..." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r64 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "You can see the graves of many famous artists and scholars including Oscar Wilde, Marcel Proust, Georges-Pierre Seurat, Eugène Delacroix, and James Morrison." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r65 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Nur içinde yatın Ahmet Kaya, Yılmaz Güney...." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r66 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Ne pas oublier de prendre un plan." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r67 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Oscar was Wilde!" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r68 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Smiths Not Dead" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r69 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Muito bonito! Realmente impressionante..." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r70 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "The ghost of a French prime minister is said to yank on your clothes if you get too close. But where else will I get to meet Jim Morrison's ghost? Hotel Reco: http://bit.ly/HnWHhz" ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

review:83486_r71 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Ahmet Kaya, Yilmaz Guney, Charlie Chaplin, Edith Piaf, Marcel Proust dahil binlerce unlunun yattigi meshur mezarlik.Sato gibi mezarlari, mumlari ve cicekleriyle kesinlikle gorulmeye deger." ;
    schema:about place:83486 .

